course: dictionary
lesson: 3005
title: Dust: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dust is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Please dust the shelves before tea» means wipe the dirt off with a cloth, because shelves are things you clean.
explain: Dust can also be a verb, a doing word. «Dust the cake with a little sugar» means sprinkle a fine powder on it. The sugar is the clue: you do not wipe sugar off a cake. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Dust as a noun means very tiny bits of dirt, skin, hair and fibres. «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide» uses the noun. The sentence tells you what the dust is made of, and that helps you picture it.
explain: Phrases use dust in special ways. «The old book had gathered dust for years» does not mean real dust. It means nobody had used the book for a long time. When a phrase puzzles you, read the whole sentence and ask what it is really saying.
fact: Dust is a noun that is uncountable: you say some dust, not a dust.
fact: To dust means to wipe dust off something, like a shelf, or to sprinkle a fine powder on something, like sugar on a cake.
fact: Dust can also be fine dry soil or powder, like the dust on a dirt road.
fact: «Dust» can make people sneeze, especially people with allergies or asthma.
fact: Phrases with dust include «dust off», «covered in dust», «a cloud of dust», «gather dust» and «bite the dust».
exercise: «Please dust the shelves before tea.» What does dust mean here? | To sweep the floor with a broom | To fill a jar with sand | To sprinkle a fine powder on something | *To wipe dust off with a cloth
exercise: Mum says, «Dust the cake with a little sugar.» What does dust mean? | *To sprinkle a fine powder on something | To wipe dirt off with a cloth | To bake it for longer | To clean a shelf with a duster
exercise: A cloud of dust rose behind the bus on the dirt road. What is the dust? | Sugar sprinkled on a cake | Wet mud on the road | *Fine dry soil or powder | Tiny bits of skin and hair
test: Which phrase with dust means that something is left unused for a long time? | *Gather dust | Bite the dust | Dust off the shelf | Cover in dust
test: Which of these is the best meaning of dust in «The dust on the Moon is studied by astronauts»? | *Very tiny bits of dirt that settle on things | A loud storm in the desert | Bright light from the Sun | Small animals that live in holes
exam: Which sentence uses dust as a verb? | *Mum will dust the shelf before the guests come | Space dust is studied by astronauts | The dust settled on the attic floor | Dust storms happen in deserts
